      "body": "More minimal reproducer:\n```python\nimport io\n\nres = bytearray(2)\nraw = io.BytesIO()\nraw.seek(2**63 - 1)\n_ = raw.readinto(res)\n```\n\nThere's an assert that `self->pos` (2**63-1) + `len` (2) should not overflow, but there should probably be an error emitted (or update to handle larger sizes):\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/blob/807db68ddd8572cfa825373bc13461b02691f4d9/Modules/_io/bytesio.c#L616-L617\n",
